6.6. Elliptic Curve Method
The P 1 methods nd a factor p of N if either p 1 is suciently smooth.
However they fail if both p ; 1 and p + 1 have large prime factors. This
happens frequently for example, both (p ; 1)=4 and (p + 1)=6 are primes for
p = 29 173 317 653 893. In 1985, Hendrik Lenstra, Jr. ?] overcame
this diculty when he announced a similar method called the Elliptic Curve
Method, abbreviated ECM.
  An elliptic curve over a eld K of characteristic not 2 is the set of solutions
(x y) 2 K  K to a cubic equation
