7.4. Continued fraction method
The continued fraction method (abbreviated CFRAC) is no longer in contention
as a modern factoring method, but we include it because it is similar to some
modern methods and easier to understand. It was used to factor the seventh
Fermat number (39 digits) in 1970 10, p. 184]:
