They used about 30 workstations at OSU over an 8{week period during spring
and summer, 1993. The researchers gathered 8.98 million relations, but were
unable to process the data and nd the factorization. During 1993{1994, while
Montgomery was at CWI, the Computational Number Theory group at CWI
completed the linear algebra and square root phases of the work. They found
the factorization N162 = p44  p119 , where
      N162 = 82 2196205286 5970195266 0120743076 1004273909
