The special algebraic form of N162 simplied the polynomial selection phase.
This beat the 158{digit record, which A.K. Lenstra and Dan Bernstein had
previously achieved using NFS.
  The OSU team also sieved the following 105{digit cofactor of 3367 ; 1:
